{"description": "🧙‍♀️  Move Fast and Break Nothing. End-to-end typesafe APIs made easy. ", "homepage": "https://tRPC.io", "topics": ["typescript", "api", "nextjs", "prisma", "next", "react"], "pushed_at": "2026-11-27T18:47:37Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-27T21:47:11Z", "detail": {"avatar": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/78011399?v=4", "license": "MIT", "discussions_total": 946, "latest_release": {"name": "v11.32.2", "tag": "v11.32.2", "published_at": "2026-11-27T16:53:43Z", "body": "## @trpc/openapi\n\n### Fixes\n\n* fix(openapi): don't require the data of a response that may be undefined by @pengzh1 in https://github.com/trpc/trpc/pull/8220\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/trpc/trpc/compare/v11.32.1...v11.32.2\n", "is_prerelease": false}, "hot_issues": [{"number": 3297, "title": "feat: Support RSC & App Layouts", "comments": 62, "created_at": "2022-11-27T16:10:39Z"}, {"number": 1963, "title": "Add a way to access the `ctx` in the `input` parsers", "comments": 34, "created_at": "2022-06-07T10:56:39Z"}, {"number": 1290, "title": "👋 Who's using tRPC? ", "comments": 23, "created_at": "2021-11-19T12:46:16Z"}, {"number": 3958, "title": "docs: recommendations on how to handle \"dependency injection\"", "comments": 18, "created_at": "2023-03-09T15:59:14Z"}, {"number": 5004, "title": "feat: publishing AppRouter without hassle", "comments": 10, "created_at": "2023-11-05T20:41:41Z"}, {"number": 6978, "title": "feat: Bind return type of a procedure to the input type of the `output` schema", "comments": 9, "created_at": "2025-10-18T15:01:44Z"}, {"number": 6306, "title": "feat: Better structural sharing in tanstack-query", "comments": 9, "created_at": "2024-12-10T16:39:15Z"}, {"number": 6950, "title": "feat: support using fetchEventSource for subscriptions", "comments": 8, "created_at": "2025-09-17T22:39:55Z"}], "discussions": [{"number": 8122, "title": "Naming traces per tRPC procedure instead of /api/trpc/[trpc]: what we see today and a middleware question", "comments": 0, "category": "Show and tell", "created_at": "2026-11-18T04:13:29Z"}, {"number": 8045, "title": "Open-source verification stack for AI-assisted TypeScript & tRPC apps (92-rule security scanner, headless Playwright QA & 72-rule UI linter)", "comments": 0, "category": "Show and tell", "created_at": "2026-11-13T21:31:59Z"}, {"number": 7622, "title": "You're really slow for the age of AI", "comments": 3, "category": "General", "created_at": "2026-10-01T07:01:47Z"}, {"number": 7566, "title": "A11yKit: End-to-End Type Safety Meets Web Accessibility (WCAG 2.2) Auditing for Full-Stack tRPC Apps", "comments": 0, "category": "Show and tell", "created_at": "2026-09-08T05:49:20Z"}, {"number": 7528, "title": "getMessageFromUnknownError test asserts against a local copy, not the live implementation", "comments": 3, "category": "Q&A", "created_at": "2026-08-28T17:51:36Z"}, {"number": 7463, "title": "Idempotent tRPC mutations, deduped on the input", "comments": 0, "category": "Show and tell", "created_at": "2026-08-09T16:19:13Z"}, {"number": 7456, "title": "`eridu-tech` — the server-side infrastructure behind your tRPC procedures", "comments": 0, "category": "Show and tell", "created_at": "2026-08-04T21:58:59Z"}, {"number": 7421, "title": "Feedback request: AI PR descriptions for TypeScript API frameworks", "comments": 1, "category": "Show and tell", "created_at": "2026-06-27T18:14:13Z"}], "readme": "<a href=\"https://trpc.io/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n  <picture>\n    <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://assets.trpc.io/www/trpc-readme-dark.png\" />\n    <img alt=\"tRPC\" src=\"https://assets.trpc.io/www/trpc-readme.png\" />\n  </picture>\n</a>\n\n<div align=\"center\">\n  <h1>tRPC</h1>\n  <h3>Move fast and break nothing.<br />End-to-end typesafe APIs made easy.</h3>\n  <a href=\"https://codecov.io/gh/trpc/trpc\">\n    <img alt=\"codecov\" src=\"https://codecov.io/gh/trpc/trpc/branch/main/graph/badge.svg?token=KPPS918B0G\">\n  </a>\n  <a href=\"https://npmcharts.com/compare/@trpc/server?interval=30\">\n    <img alt=\"weekly downloads\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/npm/dm/%40trpc/server.svg\">\n  </a>\n  <a href=\"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/blob/main/LICENSE\">\n    <img alt=\"MIT License\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/github/license/trpc/trpc\" />\n  </a>\n  <a href=\"https://trpc.io/discord\">\n    <img alt=\"Discord\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/discord/867764511159091230?color=7389D8&label&logo=discord&logoColor=ffffff\" />\n  </a>\n  <a href=\"https://x.com/trpcio\">\n    <img alt=\"Follow @trpcio on X\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/%40trpcio-000000?logo=x&logoColor=ffffff\" />\n  </a>\n  <br />\n  <br />\n  <figure>\n    <img src=\"https://assets.trpc.io/www/v10/v10-dark-landscape.gif\" alt=\"Demo\" />\n    <figcaption>\n      <p align=\"center\">\n        The client above is <strong>not</strong> importing any code from the server, only its type declarations.\n      </p>\n    </figcaption>\n  </figure>\n</div>\n\n<br />\n\n## Intro\n\ntRPC lets you build and consume fully typesafe APIs without schemas or code generation.\n\n### Features\n\n- 🧙‍♂️&nbsp; Full static typesafety and autocompletion on the client, for inputs, outputs, and errors.\n- 🐎&nbsp; No code generation, runtime bloat, or build pipeline.\n- 🍃&nbsp; Zero dependencies and a tiny client-side footprint.\n- 🐻&nbsp; Easy to add to an existing project.\n- 🔋&nbsp; Adapters for Next.js, Express, Fastify, AWS Lambda, Fetch and more, plus TanStack Query integration. Not tied to React; see the [community add-ons](https://trpc.io/docs/community/awesome-trpc).\n- 🥃&nbsp; Subscriptions over SSE and WebSockets.\n- ⚡️&nbsp; Request batching: queries made at the same time can be combined into one request, and so can mutations.\n- ✅&nbsp; Well-tested and production ready.\n\n## Quickstart\n\nBootstrap a full-stack Next.js app from the [`next-prisma-starter`](./examples/next-prisma-starter) example:\n\n```sh\nnpx create-next-app --example https://github.com/trpc/trpc --example-path examples/next-prisma-starter trpc-prisma-starter\n```\n\nSwap `npx create-next-app` for `pnpm create next-app`, `yarn create next-app` or `bunx create-next-app` if you prefer. More starters are in [`./examples`](./examples) and on the [example apps](https://trpc.io/docs/example-apps) page.\n\n**👉 Read the full documentation on [trpc.io](https://trpc.io/docs). 👈**\n\n## Contributing\n\nRead the [Contributing Guidelines](./CONTRIBUTING.md) before opening an issue or PR; they cover the branching strategy and local setup. Questions are welcome on [Discord](https://trpc.io/discord).\n\n<a href=\"https://github.com/trpc/trpc/graphs/contributors\">\n  <p align=\"center\">\n    <img width=\"720\" src=\"https://contrib.rocks/image?repo=trpc/trpc\" alt=\"A table of avatars from the project's contributors\" />\n  </p>\n</a>\n\n## Sponsors\n\nIf you enjoy working with tRPC and want to support us, consider giving a token appreciation by [GitHub Sponsors](https://trpc.io/sponsor)!\n\n<!-- SPONSORS:LIST:START -->\n<!-- oxfmt-ignore-start -->\n<!-- markdownlint-disable -->\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://trpc.io/sponsor#sponsors\"><img src=\"https://trpc.io/og/_/sponsor-cloud.png\" width=\"600\" alt=\"tRPC's sponsors, each drawn bigger the more they've given\"/></a>\n</p>\n\n### Silver partners\n\n<table>\n  <tr>\n   <td align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.coderabbit.ai/?utm_source=github&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;ref=trpc&amp;utm_campaign=trpc\"><img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4&amp;s=300\" width=\"150\" alt=\"CodeRabbit\"/><br />CodeRabbit</a></td>\n   <td align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://greptile.com/?ref=trpc&amp;utm_source=github&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=trpc\"><img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/140149887?v=4&amp;s=300\" width=\"150\" alt=\"Greptile\"/><br />Greptile</a></td>\n   <td align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://serpapi.com/?ref=trpc&amp;